                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "First of all, the controls are awful. Yeah, you can remap them, but the controls give you a window into the mind of the dev. They're completely thoughtless. This is a dumb cashgrab game. If they designed it right, it would be a 6 hour thing to 100%. Instead, they scaled it in such a screwed up way that you're going to have to cheese it. And unlike a lot of other incremental games, leaving it on while you go to bed to accumulate stuff while you sleep is not going to be enough for you to cheese your way into beating the game. They actually want you to suffer. And when I say suffer, I mean play this awful game they made. No matter how much improvements you sing into your ship, 4 missiles will blow you up and you'll lose all of your bonuses. Want to make more money to improve your ship? Enemies just leveled up despite your ship not actually getting any stronger. Not worth your time or money.",
